  spec: "[TSON-DATA] §2.6"
  description: "The same question at a map key, where §2.6 states the rule outright -- key identity is the decoded value. A resolver error rather than a validation one, as every duplicate-key vector at the reader layer is: the rule is §2.6's and not the schema's, and the schema here only supplies the key type. A processor comparing decoded text keys correctly can still miss this one, the two rules being one rule only if something owns the comparison."
